207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 192 0 R
/T (1. Hackathon Objectives)
/E (1. Hackathon Objectives)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (Australia is entering a period of significant workforce transformation as digital technologies and Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) reshape how organisations operate. While recent Australian Government research suggests that Generative AI is currently augmenting rather than replacing jobs, employers continue to face persistent workforce shortages, with the national vacancy fill rate remaining at only 68.2% in March 2026. These trends highlight a growing demand for graduates and professionals who can combine technical capability with critical thinking and practical problem-solving. \(Australian Government, 2026; Jobs and Skills Australia, 2026\).)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (Australia's higher education sector plays a critical role in developing this future workforce. Between January and May 2026, 680,582 international students studied in Australia, while Higher Education enrolments continued to grow despite broader declines across other education sectors. As student cohorts become increasingly diverse, universities are placing greater emphasis on career readiness, industry engagement and preparing graduates for an AI-enabled workforce. \(Department of Education, 2026\).)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (At the same time, AI is rapidly moving from experimentation to enterprise adoption. According to KPMG's Global Tech Report 2026, 53% of organisations report that they still lack the talent needed to deliver digital transformation successfully, while 92% believe managing AI agents will become an important workforce capability within the next five years. These findings demonstrate that future professionals will need more than technical knowledge. They must be able to apply AI responsibly to solve real-world challenges. \(KPMG, 2026\).)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (The MentorME Futura Remix Hackathon was created in response to these emerging opportunities. Through real-world Australian challenge statements, participants will tackle problems that reflect their own education, careers and communities while developing practical experience in AI, collaboration and innovation. By the end of the hackathon, participants will have strengthened their ability to identify meaningful problems, design user-centred solutions and build capabilities that are increasingly valued in Australia's future workforce.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
